{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "customer-auth-collection",
    "name": "Customer Auth",
    "description": "# Customer Auth Postman Collection\n\nThis collection contains all customer authentication endpoints implemented via Better Auth.\n\n## Important Notes & Guidelines\n\n### 1. Cookie-Based Sessions & Execution Order\nThis application uses HTTP-only cookie-based sessions (`better-auth.session_token`). Postman's built-in cookie jar automatically manages cookies between requests.\n- **Run requests in order**: Execute requests sequentially (e.g. Sign Up / Sign In → Get Session → Sign Out).\n- Do not run requests in isolation, as session endpoints depend on the session cookie established in previous steps.\n\n### 2. Avoid Collision on Repeat Runs\nSince `customerEmail` and `customerPhone` are fixed environment variables, re-running **Sign Up** after a successful registration will fail with a \"User already exists\" error (HTTP 400/422). This is expected behavior.\n- To re-run the full sequence from Sign Up, update `customerEmail` and `customerPhone` in your environment.\n- Alternatively, skip straight to the **Sign In** requests to test an existing account.\n\n### 3. Pre-Request Script (Origin Header)\nAn `Origin` header setting (`{{customerOrigin}}`) is automatically applied to all requests via a folder pre-request script to ensure CORS and trusted origin verification pass consistently.\n\n### 4. Manual Step for OTP Verification\n`Send Phone OTP` logs the generated OTP code to the server's console. Copy the OTP code from the backend server console log and paste it into the `otpCode` environment variable before executing **Verify Phone OTP**.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Customer Auth",
      "description": "Endpoints for Customer Authentication using Better Auth.",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const origin = pm.environment.get('customerOrigin') || 'http://localhost:3000';",
              "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Origin', value: origin });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Sign Up",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains user ID', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const userId = jsonData.user ? (jsonData.user.id || jsonData.user._id) : (jsonData.id || jsonData._id);",
                  "    pm.expect(userId, 'User ID should be present in response').to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.environment.set('lastUserId', userId);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"{{customerName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPassword}}\",\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{customerPhone}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/sign-up/email",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "sign-up",
                "email"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Registers a new customer account using name, email, password, and phone number.\n\n**Response:** Returns session token and user object. Session cookie is saved in Postman cookie jar automatically."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Send Phone OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{customerPhone}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/phone-number/send-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "phone-number",
                "send-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Triggers sending a phone verification OTP code.\n\n**Note:** In development mode, the OTP code is output in the server console logs and not returned in the API response. Copy the code from the server logs and paste it into the `otpCode` environment variable before running step 3."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Verify Phone OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Phone verification successful', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const isStatusTrue = jsonData.status === true;",
                  "    const isPhoneVerified = jsonData.phoneNumberVerified === true || (jsonData.user && jsonData.user.phoneNumberVerified === true);",
                  "    pm.expect(isStatusTrue || isPhoneVerified, 'Expected response to reflect phone verification success').to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{customerPhone}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{otpCode}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/phone-number/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "phone-number",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Verifies the phone number using the OTP code.\n\n**Note:** `otpCode` has no automated source (it is console-logged on the server). Set the `otpCode` variable in your environment manually after running step 2."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Get Session (whoami)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains valid customer session and user profile', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData, 'Response should contain user object').to.have.property('user');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData, 'Response should contain session object').to.have.property('session');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/get-session",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "get-session"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fetches active session details and current authenticated customer user profile.\n\n**Requires:** Valid session cookie sent via browser cookie jar."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Sign Out",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Sign out successful', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (jsonData.success !== undefined) {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    }",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/sign-out",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "sign-out"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs out the customer and invalidates the session cookie."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Sign In (Email + Password)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains user ID matching lastUserId', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const userId = jsonData.user ? (jsonData.user.id || jsonData.user._id) : (jsonData.id || jsonData._id);",
                  "    pm.expect(userId, 'User ID should be present in response').to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "",
                  "    const lastUserId = pm.environment.get('lastUserId');",
                  "    if (lastUserId) {",
                  "        pm.expect(userId, 'User ID should match lastUserId from previous auth step').to.equal(lastUserId);",
                  "    } else {",
                  "        pm.environment.set('lastUserId', userId);",
                  "    }",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/sign-in/email",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "sign-in",
                "email"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signs in an existing customer using email and password."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Sign In (Phone + Password)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains user ID matching lastUserId', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const userId = jsonData.user ? (jsonData.user.id || jsonData.user._id) : (jsonData.id || jsonData._id);",
                  "    pm.expect(userId, 'User ID should be present in response').to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "",
                  "    const lastUserId = pm.environment.get('lastUserId');",
                  "    if (lastUserId) {",
                  "        pm.expect(userId, 'User ID should match lastUserId from previous auth step').to.equal(lastUserId);",
                  "    } else {",
                  "        pm.environment.set('lastUserId', userId);",
                  "    }",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{customerPhone}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/sign-in/phone-number",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "sign-in",
                "phone-number"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signs in an existing customer using phone number and password."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "8. Trigger Email Verification",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\",\n  \"callbackURL\": \"{{frontendCallbackUrl}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/auth/send-verification-email",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "customers",
                "auth",
                "send-verification-email"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Triggers sending a verification email to the customer with a callback URL."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cart",
      "description": "Endpoints for Customer Cart management.",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const origin = pm.environment.get('customerOrigin') || 'http://localhost:3000';",
              "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Origin', value: origin });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Get Cart",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response returns cart object', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('data');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/customers/cart",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "customers",
                "cart"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Gets (or creates) the authenticated customer's cart.\n\n**Note:** Depends on an active session cookie established by running a Sign In request first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Add Item to Cart",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Cart item added successfully', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('items');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"variantId\": \"{{variantId}}\",\n  \"quantity\": 1\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/customers/cart/items",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "customers",
                "cart",
                "items"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Adds a product variant to the customer's cart.\n\n**Note:** Depends on an active session cookie established by running a Sign In request first."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
